In article <3nqdes$172a@serra.unipi.it>,
Dr.F.Mencaraglia <menca@iroe.iroe.fi.cnr.it> wrote:
>We are trying to add a magneto optical disk to out alpha station; the
>disk a a 1.3G from Sony (sony smo-f521-00). The problem is how to do
>this; I understand that we need some information to put in a disktab
>file so I looked in the ftp.digital.com file suggested in the FAQ but
>I could not finad any entry for the Sony.
>
>Has anybody successfully installed such a device and is willing to share
>the information? Or has anybody sonme helpful suggestion for solving
>the problem?
>

I have done this successfully with an HP C1716T, but I have never seen anyone
post an indication that they had made a Sony drive work.  I am appending here
a complete set of instructions for doing this with the HP drive.  To get this
done for the Sony, you will have to figure out exactly how to get it to 
identify itself as a SCSI device type 0 (= hard disk) instead of type 7 
(= optical).  You may need to get a hardware manual for the Sony drive to find
that out, though perhaps you can get this information from Sony support.  The
tail end of this post has a disklabel setup for the 1.2 GByte cartridges (which
are really ~600 MBytes/side).  Note that you have to use the 512 Byte/sector
format cartridges.

Good luck...and if you succeed, please post here.  Others have asked this same
question, but no one has ever posted a solution for a Sony drive.

==============================================================================


This is a first pass at a set of instructions for making an HP C1716T work on
a DEC Alpha under OSF/1.  It assumes that the reader already knows how to add
a normal third party SCSI disk drive to the system.  What is being described is
how to get the C1716 to identify itself as a winchester drive, not as an optical
device.


First of all, you must have the HP C1716 attached to the SCSI bus.  This example
is based on the C1716 being device 3 on SCSI bus 0.  Having done that, you must
enter superuser mode to use the "scu" facility[man pages section 8].

First, enter "scu".

  # scu

Then set the "nexus" to the appropriate SCSI address:
  scu> set nexus bus 0 target 3 lun 0

Verify that you have it set to what you want:
  scu> show nexus
  Device Nexus: Bus: 0, Target: 3, Lun: 0, Device Type: Optical

Show page # 0x21 of the C1716.  Should look something like this(note this is
more than one screen full unless you have a hugh monitor):
  scu> show page code 0x21
  
  Unknown Page Parameters (Page 21 - current values):
  
  Mode Parameter Header:
  
                   Mode Data Length: 23
                        Medium Type: 0x3
          Device Specific Parameter: 0x10
            Block Descriptor Length: 8
  
  Mode Parameter Block Descriptor:
  
                       Density Code: 0xa
           Number of Logical Blocks: 1163336
               Logical Block Length: 512
  
  Page Header:
                          Page Code: 0x21
                 Parameters Savable: Yes
                        Page Length: 10
                             Byte 2: 0x42
                             Byte 3: 0x8
                             Byte 4: 0
                             Byte 5: 0
                             Byte 6: 0x3
                             Byte 7: 0xe8
                             Byte 8: 0x2
                             Byte 9: 0x96
                            Byte 10: 0x5
                            Byte 11: 0
  

What has to be changed is the least significant bit of "byte 2" of page 0x21.
This is done as follows.  Note that the bytes are displayed one at a time.  If
you just hit return, the byte is unchanged, otherwise enter a new value.:
  scu> change pages code 0x21
  
  Changing Unknown Page Parameters (Page 21 - current values):
  
  Byte 2 [R:0-0xff D:0x42]: 0x43
  Byte 3 [R:0-0xff D:0x8]:
  Byte 4 [R:0-0xff D:0]:
