Matthias,

The best way to get version of the DEC C compiler (aka 
"cc -migrate") is to generate a source listing and look 
at the banner.
 > cc -migrate -source_listing foo.c
 > grep "DEC C" foo.lis
       Source Listing   25-Apr-1995 10:48:14   DEC C V4.2-002     
                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  
(line edited for clarity)
 
I'm not an authority on the acc ("cc") compiler, but I 
believe the best way to get its version number is to 
generate a .o file, and run file on it.
 > kikkin> grep "DEC C" foo.lis
       Source Listing   25-Apr-1995 10:48:14   DEC C V4.2-002     
                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   
> cc -c foo.c -o foo.o
> file foo.o
foo.o:  COFF format alpha executable or object module not stripped
 - version 3.11-8
   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
(line wrapped for clarity)


Tom

