In article <3n5sm5$rgb@kodak.rdcs.Kodak.COM>, Ron Huber <huber@image.kodak.com> says:
>
>Does anyone have any experience with Decsafe and OSF. It sounds ideal 
>for what I want to do. I want to have two alphas act as hot backups for 
>each other and have one automatically pick up serving the other's disk 
>when that system goes down. It sounds great but does it work.
>
>Any comments would be welcome.
>
>Ron

Ron, We set up a test with DecSafe enviornment last fall and found that NFS would 
failed over in less than 5 seconds.  The way we tested this was by having a 
third workstation which was NFS mounted to the DecSafe server conitually 
cat a file on the mounted file system.  We then pulled the network cable
out of the back of DecSafe server.  The other server picked up the NFS mount 
within the 5 seconds.  Next we tested Oracle and seeing that Oracle has to 
startup on the secondary server it took a whole 40 seconds to failover.  We
have 4 2100's and a sw800 storage works box that we are putting into place 
within the next month or 2 with the DecSafe  environment.  We are counting 
on this to provide high availability for both NFS and Oracle.  I hope this 
helps you in your decision.

Bob



