In article <3njlnv$68@amhux3.amherst.edu>, Paul D. Chapin wrote:

Paul> I'm trying to use NIS to share passwords between two DEC3000s both
Paul> running OSF/1 V3.2.  However, when I try to start the client ypbind,
Paul> the following message comes up on the console,

Paul> ypbind: Secure mode sunos 3.x servers rejected.

[...]

Paul> Neither machine is running enhanced security, although both had
Paul> enhanced security turned on at one point.

Taking your statements together, and assuming you didn't omit
anything relevant, then your server is running 'normal' NIS, but
the client is still trying to use 'secure' NIS.  That combination
will cause all NIS lookups from that client to fail.

To fix it, either re-run nissetup to remove the '-s' flag, or
cheat and edit /etc/rc.config to update the value of NIS_ARGS.

