:
: What has DEC done to stop LAT working in V3.0 ?  A bug, some new item
: to configure, or something else ?

Wouldn't that be something if we just decided to ship LAT in a non-working
state?  ;-)  I can personally vouch for the fact that "it is working".  On
the other hand, have you stumbled onto a bug?  That I can't say for sure,
based on what you've told me below.

: When trying to connect to an OSF/1 V3.0b box from a terminal server,
: I get the message "Service Disabled", yet when I do a "SHOW SERVICE" it
: tells me that the service status is "Available" and when I do a
: "SHOW SERVICE service-name" it tells me it has a status of "Reachable" and
: a rating of 254 or 253 (depending on the node I try).  Our one remaining
: node with OSF/1 V2.0 installed (our Pathworks server running 5.0) shows
: the same except its rating is 255, AND we can connect to it OK.

I've seen this type of behavior on our test configurations, it usually has 
something to do with one of the following:

	- Not enough gettys spawned on the OSF/1 LAT host OR gettys aren't
	  respawning correctly (this is a bug in the kernel _exit() code and
	  requires a patch)
	- Terminal server is having a bad day and should be rebooted. (there's
	  an entire LAT implementation running in there, too - it can have
	  problems as well)

Contact your system administrator and ask him/her to have a look.

