In article <3n54fi$qbu@sirio.cineca.it>, 
infor@meteo1.arpamet.regione.emilia-romagna.it (Franco Screpanti) writes:
>I have a ftp question. I work with a VAX running VMS 5.5-2 and FORTRAN 6.0 
>and a AXP running OSF1 2.0  and FORTRAN 3.4 . I have to transfer some 
>unformatted files created on AXP : OPEN (unit=01,file='xxx.x',type='unknown',
>form='unformatted',recordtype='segmented',recl=510) - to a VAX VMS and read 
>these files in the same segmented unformatted manner :
>OPEN(unit=01,file='xxx.x',type='old',form='unformatted',recordtype='segmented')
[snip]
>but on VAX the resulting file is with :
>RECORD FORMAT : variable length, maximum 512 bytes
>instead i need a file with :
>RECORD FORMAT : variable length .

I suspect what you actually have on the VAX is fixed length records.  
All you should need to do is change the file attributes to variable-length
records.  Since you're running VMS 5.5-2, I'll suggest Joe Meadows' FILE
utility which is available at ftp.wku.edu.  You're ahead of the game in
that you used recordtype='segmented' on the OSF system - this is exactly
the same layout as DEC Fortran on VMS uses for that recordtype.

