Ken Cameron (kcameron@gateway.ctg.com) wrote:

: the ifconfig command mentions an 'alias' option for putting more than
: one address on an interface. I tried it and for the address part that
: seems to work. But what about the issue of subnet mask and broadcast address??
: I can't seem to get those to 'alias' too. Has anyone done this type of thing
: before?? Is this at all possible?? Without needing a second interface card??

The aliased addresses are only used to determine if incoming packets are
for "this" host.  Therefore, the subnet mask and the broadcast address
aren't valid.  If you switch the address of this machine to the Class B
machine with an alias for the Class A address, you will need to play some
games with the routes (I'd recommend just bouncing all the class A stuff
of a convenient router) to get it to work.

-Ron



