I'm having a problem with DEC OSF/1 V3.0 Worksystem Software (Rev. 347)
on a DEC Alpha machine.  The problem occurs when I set up a .forward
file to pipe incoming mail to a perl script e.g.

         "|/usr/local/etc/gopher/gmail"

This always results in:

   ----- The following addresses had delivery problems -----
   "| /usr/work/gopherlib/.sup/gmail/rungmail"  (unrecoverable error)
    (expanded from: <gmail@alpha1.csd.uwm.edu>)
     
   ----- Transcript of session follows -----
   sh: 32481 Memory fault - core dumped
   554 "| /usr/work/gopherlib/.sup/gmail/rungmail"... unknown mailer
     error 139

The purpose of the perl script is to insert the mailed message into
a gopher hierarchy.  The error occurs using both perl 4.037 and
perl 5.000.  The same perl scripts work OK on an RS/6000 using
perl 4.036 and perl 5.001+.

Thinking it was a perl problem, I wrote a short C program to read
stdin and write it to a temporary file.  This program causes the
same error when the stdin is piped from mail.  So the problem
doesn't necessarily involve perl.  As a further test, I ran both
the perl script and the C program manually, piping a test file
into them; e.g.

   cat test.file | /usr/local/etc/gopher/gmail

The programs work perfectly OK run in this manner.

It appears to me that there is a problem with OSF1 when piping
incoming mail to any kind of program.  Has anyone else run into
this problem?  If so, is there a fix or circumvention?

Thanks in advance for any insight you can contribute.

-- 
