In article <3nbh29$k1i@hydra.cc.umb.edu>,
Ted Corning <kismet@trantor.cc.umb.edu> wrote:
>
>First, a question. To get things started up when the system boots, I have
>been putting entries into the /etc/inittab file. Is this the right place
>to put them? I haven't found any place in the documentation where this is
>covered very well.

It's usually better to put things into /sbin/init.d, with appropriate
symbolic links from /sbin/rc3.d.  That way, your new entries are only
executed when going into multi-user mode, which is usually what you want.
(There are some exceptions, of course.)

