(Sami Laari) writes:

|>We are searching for Multimedia tools running on DEC OSF/1. We expect the 
|>tools to be able to use HMTL or SGML format. We use Motif and intend to 
|>embed multimedia in our application.

Digital bundles Multimedia Services for DEC OSF/1 (that name will obviously
change soon) with its Unix workstations, but it mostly provides simple tools
to record and playback audio and video.  They can be used to good effect as
multimedia helper apps for a Web browser to view MPEG & AVI movies, playback
audio clips, etc, but they don't understand SGML or HTML directly themselves.

Depending on what level you want to integrate multimedia with your application,
you can invoke the existing programs from your application, or roll your own
support by calling the library directly yourself, or use a more extensive
"authoring" package like Aimtech's IconAuthor or MetaCard's MetaCard.

Without more details about what you are trying to do, it's hard to be more
specific, but hopefully this will get you moving in the right direction.

