organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Your installed kernel does not know about the addional cards yet. This
is a size optimiation in that the kernel does not have unused table
entries for this and many other kernel table. The down side of this
optimisation is that you have to rebuild the kernel if you install 
new feature hardware. You can verify this with the command:

sizer -gt

which will show just one graphics card is seen and not three.

To rebuild your kernel (the easy way):

boot using genvmunix as your kernel.

Build a new kernel using :
	doconfig -c HOSTNAME
(where HOSTNAME is your machine name in caps.)
Install the new kernel in /

reboot using the new kernel.

The X server will automatically use the new screens. The mouse will
properly travere the screens in card order. If you don't like the order
of the cards, you can configure the X server to reorder the screens.

/Dave

