X-Deja-AN: 100431483
references: <1995Apr13.163219.4907@vtf.idx.com>
organization: Duchy of Wabesylvan Obspauk
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

In article <1995Apr13.163219.4907@vtf.idx.com> mll@hawkeye.idx.com (Matthew Labbe) writes:

Matt> I've just installed OSF/1 V2.0 on this tiny Alpha box and
Matt> I'm having a hard time wading through this enhanced
Matt> security stuff.

That's partly because of using 2.0, of course.  If you have any
choice at all, I'd really recommend v3.2.

Matt> My problem today is getting the message:

Matt> "Audit control failure"

Matt> when I try to run XSysAdmin or XIsso.  Auditing is
Matt> configured and running.

These two statements are incompatible.  You have run
"auditsetup", but auditing is NOT configured and running *in your
kernel*.  The syscall is failing with ENOSYS.

You need to add "options DEC_AUDIT" to your kernel config file,
rerun
	"doconfig -c `hostname | cut -d. -f1 | dd conv=ucase 2>/dev/null`",
install the new kernel as the new /vmunix and reboot.

--
