> >> I wrote a commentary a month or so ago in my newsletter.  The basic 
> >> premise is that DEC ought to promote the sale of el cheapo AXP 
> >> motherboards together with Linux or NetBSD.  Result: an AXP econobox that 
> >> won't compete directly with existing AXP products.  This concept is being 
> >> championed by some people in the Digital Unix group.  Accordingly, if 
