"##wengler" ??  That's the oddest password encryption I've ever seen.
I think your password is faulty.  Edit your master password file (on
the NIS master server) and replace "##wengler" with the correct
encryption of your password.  Or just delete it.  (So the line reads
"wengler::6011:...".)  Then run make to rebuild the database and push it
to any slave servers.  Now you should be able to login with no password.
Then run yppasswd to set one.

