On 15 Apr 1995, Bill Broadley wrote:

> I would like to purchase a server to run matlab, mathematica, and maple
> for a lab of 30-40 xterminals.   I'm interested in any comments on the
> 700K or the Alpha 2100, especially anything related to similar experiences.
> 
> Comments solicited on any aspect of these machines.  I'm not
> even sure if matlab, mathematica, and maple work on these machines, but
> I have queries in to the software companies.
>[...]
 
Back when we had some HP 9000/735's, we did some comparisons on the
performance of some matlab jobs between these machines and our DEC Alpha
300/500's (150MHz). The HP's are long gone now, and I don't have the exact
numbers to hand, but we found that for our jobs at least, the HP's were
not very good at matlab; a factor of something like 40% of the Alpha comes
to mind. The HP's were better at some other things, but generally we found
their performance to be extremely variable (eg some workloads were twice
as quick on the HP, while some others were only a tenth as fast). If you
want 40 xterms on one machine, you're going to need at least 256MB memory,
maybe 512, if they're all going to be active at once. 

fwiw.

