Two warnings:

1: SATAN creates its own security problems and may allow
   root permissions for non privledged while it is running.
   see the recent CERT advisory on this issue.

2: After running SATAN if you have ULTRIX machines (V4.2)
   we encountered some small problems as follows:

If you are running ultrix on your workstation could you please take a
second to check the current CPU usage of /etc/elcsd. Look
at the TT column in a ps alx output.

If you are running Ultrix 4.2 (use 'uname -s -r' to check) then you will
probably find it is using about 80% cpu. This is not normal and you can
fix the problem by logging into your workstation (as root) and typing:

'eli -d'
'eli -e'


