Sorry, but what you are doing is unsupported.  The linker on your V2.0 system
doesn't know about changes that were made to the object file format on V3.0
system.  The last digit in the version string (6 vs 4) shows which release
of the OS the object came from.  We don't support running V3.0 objects on
V2.0 systems, or in general running new objects on old systems.

In specific, the error message from the V2.0 linker is refering to the .rconst
section that was added in V3.0.  That library will only work on V3.0 and
greater systems.
