> I've got an Alpha 2100 running OSF/1 v3.0 and a Practical Peripherals 14400 v.32bis external modem.
> Can anyone help me with how to get started configuring the modem for remote dialin? Thankyou.
> 
I currently have a couple of calls outstanding with the DEC help line 
asking a similar question. Their reply so far is...

On a DEC3000/300lx the port cannot stand anymore than 9600. Any attempt at running
faster than this will result in a SILO overflow message.

On a 2100, the port should (they think) run at 19200, but they cannot
predict the results of OSF as they have only ever got satisfactory results
with speeds up to 9600.

To actually configure the OSF, you basically add a line to the /etc/inittab file that
spawns a getty. The getty then references an entry for the speed settings in the
/etc/gettydefs file (which you will see only goes up to 9600 !).

To get the exact form og the line for the inittab file, do a man on inittab.

Hope this helps,

John Hill







