Top's SIZE field includes memory-mapped devices, which on some cards
can add a lot of bogus memory (A ZLXp-E1 Xdec seems to be ~13M bigger
than a HX? Xdec in OSF/1 3.2). And I *think* that the HX? (whatever
the name of the internal graphics card in a 3000/300LX is) Xdec's SIZE
already includes a memory-map of the HX-card's memory...

Ignore it, it just *look* big. I haven't the Release Notes at hand,
but I think that this issue is addressed there.

I think the big memory-leak in Xdec was fixed in OSF/1 3.0 (or
possibly in 3.2), so you shouldn't need to add '-terminate' to the end
of the line in the Xservers file any longer (it was definitely needed
in OSF/1 2.x).

>PS: Can you swap in a file in v3.2?

Nope.



