From: kivinen@hut.fi (Tero Kivinen)
Subject: Re: advfs "no space" problem
Date: 1995/04/04
Message-ID: <KIVINEN.95Apr4181446@closenet.hut.fi>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 100804611
references: <3kmrs9$54t@westnet.westnet.com> <3lcq1d$cq9@sandbox.atcon.com>
organization: Freenet, Finland
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

In article <3lcq1d$cq9@sandbox.atcon.com> shawn@warp.atcon.com (Shawn Preston) writes:
> I see someone ellse posted on here asking if there were any dangers in
> using ADVFS with news (I have INN) . My advice is DON'T until someone
> fixs the problem. The headaches I went through I don't wish on anyone.

You ware probably out of metadata. Try defragment. It wont help, but
if it returns ENO_MORE_MCELLS (-1055) you are out of metacells.
Metadata is only allocated when the filesystem haven't got lots of
data, so if you put some big files first and then fill the rest of
filedomain with small files you can run out of it quite soon. Adding
more disk will not add metadata so it won't help.

To make more metadata, backup the whole filesystem, remove the
filedomain and recreate the filedomain. Then make enough empty files
on the filesystem and remove them before restoring the backup. For
news the suitable number of empty files seems to be about 500 000 *
1 GB of news partition. Making 1 300 000 empty files allowed about
650 000 news articles on filedomain.
