fork, and exec!

For example:

#include <stdio.h>

main() {
if (fork() == 0) {
  execve("ls","/bin/ls","-l",NULL);
  }
else {
  printf("I've forked to create a child, running ls\n");
  }
}

This is probably not right, but if you do a man fork, and a man exec, 
then it will help you.

Mark.



