Since we are blessed by so many DEC employees in our newsgroup, I have a 
question regarding DEC threads and the use of thread safe code.

To obtain thread safe code one must remove or protect references to the 
following dependencies:

	o Static (or global) read-write data
        o File descriptors shared between threads
	o REFERENCES TO GLOBAL ERRNO
	o calls to other nonthread-safe routines.


The problem is that the GLOBAL ERRNO is used by many UNIX functions, such as
file I/O, sockets, semaphores, etc..., and even the PTHREAD library. 

So, my question is, how can one write thread safe code, when a significant 
number of UNIX functions are using the GLOBAL ERRNO, which includes the PTHREAD
library? 

thanks...

