My advice is to:

- Get the complete list of applications on your machine, and check for 
availability on Alpha OSF/1. If an application isn't available, try to 
get your reseller to prove that it will work satisfactorily in a 
translated form. (I've generally been impressed with the translated 
performance).

- Get loads of memory! An AlphaStation 200 4/100 with 96Mb of memory will 
easily feel faster than an AlphaStation 200 4/233 with just 32Mb of 
memory. Memory is cheao enough for 64 or 96 Mb to be feasible.

- Think before getting a 21" Screen. I have a demo AlphaStation 400, and 
the 21" Screen, is too heavy! It also is a significant cost factor. If 
the screen is important to you, think about the 17" screen. If you just 
want a server, then get the 15" screen.

Talk to a good reseller, who can help you through the process. Buy from 
the one who looks after you best, and then they may stay in business!

